<header><p class="st-kicker">other · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Overijssel</h1><p class="st-meta">1528 CE – 1581 CE · capital Deventer</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The eastern Hanseatic lands of the former bishopric of Utrecht, with Deventer, Kampen and Zwolle, under Habsburg rule before joining the Dutch Republic.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Oversticht, the eastern part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-utrecht">Prince-Bishopric of Utrecht</a>, was ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> until 1528, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-the-palatinate">Bishop Henry of Bavaria</a> handed his temporal power to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>. Overijssel then became one of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/habsburg-netherlands">Seventeen Provinces</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drenthe">Drenthe</a> attached to it.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The province was governed by estates of nobles and the three towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deventer">Deventer</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kampen">Kampen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwolle">Zwolle</a>, Hanseatic ports on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ijssel">IJssel</a>. Deventer was the birthplace of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devotio-moderna">Devotio Moderna</a> movement and a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> ruled through stadtholders but left the towns their privileges.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Overijssel joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-utrecht">Union of Utrecht</a> in 1579 and, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-abjuration">Act of Abjuration</a> of 1581, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, although Spanish troops held parts of it until the 1590s.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lordship-of-overijssel.jpg" alt="Lordship of Overijssel" width="320" height="290"><figcaption>Image: Isaak Tirion · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Overijssel_1757.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1528 CE – 1581 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Deventer</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles V, Philip II of Spain</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch and Low Saxon</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Overijssel, Oversticht</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1554&amp;focus=lordship-of-overijssel" aria-label="Lordship of Overijssel on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4819 374 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Overijssel lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5139 630L5115 634M5139 630L5102 664M5139 630L5099 670M5139 630L5097 634"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5115 634h0M5102 664h0M5099 670h0M5097 634h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5139 630h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5139 630h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Deventer. <a href="/atlas?year=1554&amp;focus=lordship-of-overijssel">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
